.TH WHOAMI 1
.SH NAME
whoami, id, groups \- who you are
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B whoami
.br
.B id
.br
.B groups
.SH DESCRIPTION
These are commands built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
Every process runs as a user number (uid), a group number (gid) and up to
16 more groups; it never changes, and the kernel stamps it on every message
.RB ( ident (2)).
The names are in
.B /etc/users
and
.BR /etc/groups .
.TP
.B whoami
your user name
.TP
.B id
your user and group numbers with their names:
.B uid=1000(alice) gid=100(users) groups=...
.TP
.B groups
the names of your groups, the main one first
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/users
user names, numbers, homes
.TP
.B /etc/groups
group names and members
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR users (5),
.BR su (1),
.BR useradd (8)
